Event Fields Sent when <code>step_started</code> <code>step</code>, <code>label</code> A step begins. <code>label</code> is a human-readable name for display <code>progress</code> <code>step</code>, <code>current</code>, <code>total</code>, <code>message</code> A step's count advances, or its status changes. All but <code>step</code> may be absent - see below <code>step_finished</code> <code>step</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>message</code> A step ends. <code>status</code> is <code>"succeeded"</code> or <code>"failed"</code>, and a failed step carries the error in <code>message</code> <code>metric</code> <code>step</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>values</code> A step produces a result worth charting live, such as one generation of the genetic algorithm. <code>values</code> is an object of named numbers <p><code>progress</code> events</p> <ul> <li><code>current</code> and <code>total</code> are whole numbers, and <code>current</code> never exceeds <code>total</code>. <code>total</code> is absent when the amount of work is not known.</li> <li><code>message</code> is the status text shown beside a progress bar (e.g., <code>"Fold 3/5"</code>).</li> <li>A status sent during work that is not counted (e.g., <code>"Running Beagle"</code>) repeats the step's last <code>current</code> and <code>total</code>, so it should not be read as the count starting over. Before a step has counted anything, a status has no counts at all.</li> </ul> <pre><code>@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.206Z","event":"progress","step":"beagle_phase","message":"Writing VCF"}
@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.953Z","event":"progress","step":"read_vcf","current":112,"total":112,"message":"Converting genotypes"}
</code></pre> <p>Nested steps</p> <p>Steps can run inside other steps. For example, <code>beagle_phase_geno()</code> reads BEAGLE's output with the VCF reader, so a <code>read_vcf</code> step starts and finishes inside the <code>beagle_phase</code> step. Track steps with a stack, not a single current step: <code>progress</code> and <code>metric</code> events belong to the innermost running step, named in their <code>step</code> field.</p> <pre><code>@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.199Z","event":"step_started","step":"beagle_phase","label":"Phasing (Beagle)"}
@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.947Z","event":"step_started","step":"read_vcf","label":"Reading VCF"}
@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.987Z","event":"step_finished","step":"read_vcf","status":"succeeded"}
@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.987Z","event":"step_finished","step":"beagle_phase","status":"succeeded"}
</code></pre> <p>Failed steps</p> <pre><code>@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.988Z","event":"step_started","step":"graph_blocking","label":"Graph Blocking"}
@@HS {"v":"2.0.0","at":"2026-11-02T04:14:28.988Z","event":"step_finished","step":"graph_blocking","status":"failed","message":"geno must be supplied for a graph_strategy: the method computes LD from the genotypes directly. Pass it to def_blocks(strategy, map, geno = ...)."}
</code></pre>
